1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,700
What if a country opened its first

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:03,381
chip plants,

3
00:00:03,381 --> 00:00:04,533
celebrated,

4
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,647
and not one of them actually made

5
00:00:06,647 --> 00:00:08,187
a chip from scratch?

6
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:12,210
That is India in twenty twenty-six.

7
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,508
The government says five chip units are

8
00:00:14,508 --> 00:00:16,640
in commercial production.

9
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:19,172
But the first ones to open do

10
00:00:19,172 --> 00:00:21,500
not make chips from silicon.

11
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,897
They take chips made somewhere else and

12
00:00:23,897 --> 00:00:25,250
finish them.

13
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:25,929
And that,

14
00:00:25,929 --> 00:00:26,789
it turns out,

15
00:00:26,789 --> 00:00:28,773
may be exactly the right way to

16
00:00:28,773 --> 00:00:29,594
start.

17
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,778
What does it actually mean to make

18
00:00:42,778 --> 00:00:43,940
a chip?

19
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:52,860
Making a chip happens in two halves.

20
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:55,336
The first half is the front end,

21
00:00:55,336 --> 00:00:56,560
the fab.

22
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:57,195
Here,

23
00:00:57,195 --> 00:01:00,000
light and chemicals build billions of tiny

24
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,780
circuits onto a silicon wafer,

25
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,400
layer after layer.

26
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:06,090
It is the hardest part,

27
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:08,150
and the most expensive.

28
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:10,990
One industry study put the cost of

29
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:13,365
a state-of-the-art fab at roughly five

30
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:16,869
billion dollars to twenty billion dollars.

31
00:01:17,117 --> 00:01:19,697
The second half is the back end.

32
00:01:19,787 --> 00:01:22,839
The finished wafer is cut into individual

33
00:01:22,839 --> 00:01:23,487
chips.

34
00:01:23,487 --> 00:01:26,294
Each chip is sealed inside a protective

35
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:27,034
package,

36
00:01:27,034 --> 00:01:29,051
wired to the outside world,

37
00:01:29,051 --> 00:01:31,437
and tested before it ships.

38
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:32,428
In India,

39
00:01:32,428 --> 00:01:34,172
this is called assembly,

40
00:01:34,172 --> 00:01:34,812
testing,

41
00:01:34,812 --> 00:01:36,687
marking and packaging.

42
00:01:36,687 --> 00:01:38,192
It is skilled work,

43
00:01:38,192 --> 00:01:40,232
but it needs far less money and

44
00:01:40,232 --> 00:01:43,892
far fewer exotic machines than a fab.

45
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:47,000
Let me draw where the money is.

46
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,195
Split the value of the chip industry

47
00:01:49,195 --> 00:01:50,760
into slices.

48
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,643
Designing the chip is about half of

49
00:01:52,643 --> 00:01:53,600
the value.

50
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,169
Making the wafer in a fab,

51
00:01:55,169 --> 00:01:56,650
about a quarter.

52
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,147
Packaging and testing,

53
00:01:58,147 --> 00:01:59,810
only six percent.

54
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:02,034
So the back end is the smallest

55
00:02:02,034 --> 00:02:02,900
slice.

56
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:04,819
But it is also the one door

57
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:07,268
a newcomer can open first.

58
00:02:07,517 --> 00:02:10,372
India walked through that door in a

59
00:02:10,372 --> 00:02:12,558
town called Sanand.

60
00:02:18,217 --> 00:02:21,759
What is actually running in India today?

61
00:02:27,217 --> 00:02:29,417
Sanand is an industrial town in the

62
00:02:29,417 --> 00:02:31,047
state of Gujarat.

63
00:02:31,047 --> 00:02:33,107
In February twenty twenty-six,

64
00:02:33,107 --> 00:02:35,604
the American memory maker Micron

65
00:02:35,604 --> 00:02:38,101
inaugurated a packaging and test plant

66
00:02:38,101 --> 00:02:38,496
there,

67
00:02:38,496 --> 00:02:40,577
a project of about two point seven

68
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:42,217
five billion dollars.

69
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:44,477
It now ships memory chips.

70
00:02:44,477 --> 00:02:45,848
At the end of March,

71
00:02:45,848 --> 00:02:46,986
a second plant,

72
00:02:46,986 --> 00:02:49,286
from the Indian company Kaynes,

73
00:02:49,286 --> 00:02:51,747
started commercial operation.

74
00:02:51,747 --> 00:02:52,503
In July,

75
00:02:52,503 --> 00:02:53,065
a third,

76
00:02:53,065 --> 00:02:54,810
from a joint venture of CG Power

77
00:02:54,810 --> 00:02:57,118
with the Japanese chipmaker Renesas,

78
00:02:57,118 --> 00:02:58,687
began production.

79
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:01,564
All three in the same town.

80
00:03:01,817 --> 00:03:02,786
Inside,

81
00:03:02,786 --> 00:03:05,057
the work goes like this.

82
00:03:05,057 --> 00:03:07,997
Finished wafers arrive from fabs abroad.

83
00:03:07,997 --> 00:03:10,690
Machines cut each wafer into individual

84
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:11,497
dies.

85
00:03:11,637 --> 00:03:13,880
Each die is placed in a package,

86
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,803
connected to the outside with tiny wires,

87
00:03:16,803 --> 00:03:17,461
sealed,

88
00:03:17,461 --> 00:03:18,967
and then tested.

89
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:21,393
The machines and most of the materials

90
00:03:21,393 --> 00:03:23,485
still come from the United States,

91
00:03:23,485 --> 00:03:24,099
Japan,

92
00:03:24,099 --> 00:03:25,967
Taiwan and South Korea.

93
00:03:26,217 --> 00:03:27,679
But the factory,

94
00:03:27,679 --> 00:03:29,661
the jobs and the know-how are now

95
00:03:29,661 --> 00:03:31,004
in India.

96
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,235
In total,

97
00:03:32,235 --> 00:03:34,257
India has approved twelve chip

98
00:03:34,257 --> 00:03:36,253
manufacturing units,

99
00:03:36,253 --> 00:03:38,779
with investments worth about seventeen

100
00:03:38,779 --> 00:03:40,390
billion dollars.

101
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,990
Look at the mix.

102
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,496
One silicon fab,

103
00:03:43,496 --> 00:03:45,764
two fabs for special materials and

104
00:03:45,764 --> 00:03:46,494
displays,

105
00:03:46,494 --> 00:03:49,110
and nine packaging and test plants.

106
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,312
By September,

107
00:03:50,312 --> 00:03:51,931
the government said five of them were

108
00:03:51,931 --> 00:03:53,790
in commercial production.

109
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,352
In twenty twenty-one,

110
00:03:55,352 --> 00:03:55,997
it says,

111
00:03:55,997 --> 00:03:58,222
the country had no commercial chip plant

112
00:03:58,222 --> 00:03:59,267
at all.

113
00:03:59,517 --> 00:04:01,919
So why would a country spend billions

114
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:05,189
on the smallest slice of the business?

115
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:13,835
Why does India want chip plants at

116
00:04:13,835 --> 00:04:14,809
all?

117
00:04:19,850 --> 00:04:22,426
Because it buys an enormous amount of

118
00:04:22,426 --> 00:04:23,220
chips.

119
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,368
According to the government,

120
00:04:25,368 --> 00:04:28,022
India spent almost one hundred and fifty

121
00:04:28,022 --> 00:04:30,677
billion dollars on imported chips between

122
00:04:30,677 --> 00:04:33,690
twenty sixteen and twenty twenty-five.

123
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:36,366
Imports grew by an average of almost

124
00:04:36,366 --> 00:04:38,050
a quarter a year.

125
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:39,950
If that trend continued,

126
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:41,300
the government says,

127
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:43,818
India could be importing two hundred and

128
00:04:43,818 --> 00:04:46,108
forty billion dollars worth of chips a

129
00:04:46,108 --> 00:04:48,310
year by twenty thirty-five.

130
00:04:48,570 --> 00:04:50,103
That is a projection,

131
00:04:50,103 --> 00:04:51,370
not a fact.

132
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:53,784
But it explains the hurry.

133
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:56,160
And the need is growing.

134
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:58,467
The government projects that India's own

135
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:00,525
demand for chips will reach one hundred

136
00:05:00,525 --> 00:05:02,584
and ten billion dollars a year by

137
00:05:02,584 --> 00:05:03,704
twenty thirty,

138
00:05:03,704 --> 00:05:04,596
as phones,

139
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:05,031
cars,

140
00:05:05,031 --> 00:05:07,546
data centers and factories all fill up

141
00:05:07,546 --> 00:05:09,290
with electronics.

142
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:09,929
Again,

143
00:05:09,929 --> 00:05:11,370
a projection.

144
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:13,785
And every chip India buys abroad is

145
00:05:13,785 --> 00:05:16,068
money that leaves the country.

146
00:05:16,317 --> 00:05:18,797
And India has done this before.

147
00:05:18,797 --> 00:05:19,923
A decade ago,

148
00:05:19,923 --> 00:05:22,212
three in every four mobile phones sold

149
00:05:22,212 --> 00:05:24,147
in India were imported.

150
00:05:24,237 --> 00:05:26,743
Then factories started assembling phones

151
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:27,632
in India,

152
00:05:27,632 --> 00:05:29,827
starting with the final steps.

153
00:05:30,137 --> 00:05:31,735
By twenty twenty-five,

154
00:05:31,735 --> 00:05:33,102
the government says,

155
00:05:33,102 --> 00:05:35,650
almost every phone sold in India was

156
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:37,177
made in India.

157
00:05:37,397 --> 00:05:39,910
Packaging chips is the same first step,

158
00:05:39,910 --> 00:05:42,287
applied to the chip itself.

159
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:45,600
India also starts with a hidden strength.

160
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:48,195
The government says nearly one in five

161
00:05:48,195 --> 00:05:50,359
chip designers in the world works in

162
00:05:50,359 --> 00:05:51,440
India.

163
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:53,570
Remember the slices.

164
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,358
Design is the biggest one,

165
00:05:55,358 --> 00:05:57,584
and India already does a large part

166
00:05:57,584 --> 00:06:00,410
of it for companies around the world.

167
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,427
Packaging,

168
00:06:01,427 --> 00:06:02,592
the smallest slice,

169
00:06:02,592 --> 00:06:04,380
has now arrived.

170
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,498
The missing piece in the middle is

171
00:06:06,498 --> 00:06:07,560
the fab.

172
00:06:07,817 --> 00:06:10,788
And the fab is where things get

173
00:06:10,788 --> 00:06:12,237
harder.

174
00:06:17,883 --> 00:06:20,694
How close is India to making the

175
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:22,231
chip itself?

176
00:06:26,883 --> 00:06:28,908
India's first real chip fab is being

177
00:06:28,908 --> 00:06:32,173
built by Tata Electronics in Dholera,

178
00:06:32,173 --> 00:06:33,919
also in Gujarat,

179
00:06:33,919 --> 00:06:36,451
with technology from the Taiwanese

180
00:06:36,451 --> 00:06:38,063
chipmaker PSMC.

181
00:06:38,183 --> 00:06:40,342
It is worth about about eleven billion

182
00:06:40,342 --> 00:06:40,864
dollars,

183
00:06:40,864 --> 00:06:42,843
and it is designed for fifty thousand

184
00:06:42,843 --> 00:06:44,163
wafers a month.

185
00:06:44,273 --> 00:06:46,376
When construction began in twenty

186
00:06:46,376 --> 00:06:47,287
twenty-four,

187
00:06:47,287 --> 00:06:49,623
India's IT minister said the first chip

188
00:06:49,623 --> 00:06:51,725
would arrive in December twenty

189
00:06:51,725 --> 00:06:52,637
twenty-six,

190
00:06:52,637 --> 00:06:54,872
at twenty-eight nanometers.

191
00:06:55,117 --> 00:06:57,167
That has changed.

192
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:58,896
According to Tech Times,

193
00:06:58,896 --> 00:07:00,648
the fab will now start with older

194
00:07:00,648 --> 00:07:02,596
ninety nanometer chips,

195
00:07:02,596 --> 00:07:05,223
and commercial production is targeted for

196
00:07:05,223 --> 00:07:06,917
mid twenty twenty-eight.

197
00:07:07,357 --> 00:07:09,887
Tata and PSMC say starting with a

198
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:12,107
mature process is normal,

199
00:07:12,107 --> 00:07:15,237
and in chipmaking it often is.

200
00:07:15,567 --> 00:07:17,370
A new fab has to learn to

201
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:19,430
make good chips before it can make

202
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:20,802
small ones.

203
00:07:21,050 --> 00:07:23,777
Even the financing shows how new this

204
00:07:23,777 --> 00:07:24,650
is.

205
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,231
In February twenty twenty-six,

206
00:07:27,231 --> 00:07:29,709
the project borrowed seven hundred and

207
00:07:29,709 --> 00:07:31,963
thirty-five million dollars from a group

208
00:07:31,963 --> 00:07:34,140
of international banks.

209
00:07:34,350 --> 00:07:36,019
According to Tech Times,

210
00:07:36,019 --> 00:07:38,554
the land pledged as collateral was valued

211
00:07:38,554 --> 00:07:39,378
at zero,

212
00:07:39,378 --> 00:07:41,279
because nothing had been built on it

213
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:42,090
yet.

214
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,539
The banks were betting on the Tata

215
00:07:44,539 --> 00:07:46,684
name more than on the factory.

216
00:07:46,950 --> 00:07:50,180
But the competition will not wait.

217
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:51,433
Chinese foundries,

218
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:53,277
backed by state subsidies,

219
00:07:53,277 --> 00:07:56,077
are expanding exactly this kind of mature

220
00:07:56,077 --> 00:07:57,430
chip production.

221
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,383
One of them,

222
00:07:58,383 --> 00:07:59,091
Nexchip,

223
00:07:59,091 --> 00:08:01,533
is ramping up to one hundred thousand

224
00:08:01,533 --> 00:08:03,110
wafers a month.

225
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,950
And India carries an old scar.

226
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:07,518
In twenty oh five,

227
00:08:07,518 --> 00:08:10,441
a three billion dollar chip project called

228
00:08:10,441 --> 00:08:13,365
SemIndia stalled while its imported

229
00:08:13,365 --> 00:08:15,996
equipment sat stuck at Indian ports,

230
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:18,456
waiting for customs clearance.

231
00:08:18,717 --> 00:08:20,483
Let me draw why a fab is

232
00:08:20,483 --> 00:08:23,607
so much harder than a packaging plant.

233
00:08:23,887 --> 00:08:26,598
A packaging plant needs machines that many

234
00:08:26,598 --> 00:08:27,706
companies sell,

235
00:08:27,706 --> 00:08:31,017
and materials with ordinary purity.

236
00:08:31,417 --> 00:08:34,489
A fab needs lithography machines from one

237
00:08:34,489 --> 00:08:35,744
or two suppliers,

238
00:08:35,744 --> 00:08:38,048
gases and chemicals so pure that

239
00:08:38,048 --> 00:08:40,864
contamination is counted in parts per

240
00:08:40,864 --> 00:08:41,607
trillion,

241
00:08:41,607 --> 00:08:44,767
and engineers who have done it before.

242
00:08:45,037 --> 00:08:47,336
Every one of those still comes from

243
00:08:47,336 --> 00:08:48,396
abroad.

244
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,520
India knows this.

245
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,303
Its next move is aimed at exactly

246
00:08:53,303 --> 00:08:54,460
that list.

247
00:09:00,117 --> 00:09:03,132
What comes after packaging?

248
00:09:09,117 --> 00:09:11,153
In July twenty twenty-six,

249
00:09:11,153 --> 00:09:13,670
the government approved a second chip

250
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:15,729
program worth about thirteen billion

251
00:09:15,729 --> 00:09:16,787
dollars.

252
00:09:17,007 --> 00:09:18,125
For the first time,

253
00:09:18,125 --> 00:09:20,179
it pays companies that make the things

254
00:09:20,179 --> 00:09:21,298
behind the chips,

255
00:09:21,298 --> 00:09:22,416
the machines,

256
00:09:22,416 --> 00:09:24,904
the special chemicals and the gases,

257
00:09:24,904 --> 00:09:27,414
with an incentive of thirty percent of

258
00:09:27,414 --> 00:09:28,927
the project cost.

259
00:09:29,197 --> 00:09:29,894
Because,

260
00:09:29,894 --> 00:09:32,516
as one consultant at Kearney put it,

261
00:09:32,516 --> 00:09:34,921
the lion's share of critical inputs will

262
00:09:34,921 --> 00:09:36,340
still be imported,

263
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:39,345
even with new fabs and packaging plants.

264
00:09:39,583 --> 00:09:41,600
The new program also pays for more

265
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,025
fabs,

266
00:09:42,025 --> 00:09:44,490
covering up to forty percent of the

267
00:09:44,490 --> 00:09:46,883
cost of a new silicon fab.

268
00:09:47,053 --> 00:09:48,963
And it pays for people.

269
00:09:49,163 --> 00:09:51,000
Chip design tools are now in more

270
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,733
than three hundred Indian universities,

271
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:56,259
and the equipment maker Lam Research plans

272
00:09:56,259 --> 00:09:58,785
to help train sixty thousand fab engineers

273
00:09:58,785 --> 00:10:00,763
over the next decade.

274
00:10:01,163 --> 00:10:03,803
Because a fab is not only machines.

275
00:10:03,803 --> 00:10:05,804
It is thousands of people who know

276
00:10:05,804 --> 00:10:07,294
how to run them.

277
00:10:07,550 --> 00:10:10,238
And India is not trying to win

278
00:10:10,238 --> 00:10:11,510
on price.

279
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:13,553
Chinese mature chips are cheap and

280
00:10:13,553 --> 00:10:15,110
subsidized.

281
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:17,227
According to Tech Times,

282
00:10:17,227 --> 00:10:19,890
India's real argument is trust.

283
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:22,004
Companies in America,

284
00:10:22,004 --> 00:10:24,167
Europe and Japan want a second source

285
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:25,896
of chips in a country they see

286
00:10:25,896 --> 00:10:28,010
as a reliable partner.

287
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:31,121
That is a selling point no subsidy

288
00:10:31,121 --> 00:10:32,308
can buy.

289
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:34,755
That is the logic of the whole

290
00:10:34,755 --> 00:10:35,400
plan.

291
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,116
Start where the door is open,

292
00:10:37,116 --> 00:10:38,840
packaging and testing.

293
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,922
Learn to run clean factories,

294
00:10:40,922 --> 00:10:42,213
train engineers,

295
00:10:42,213 --> 00:10:44,080
and attract suppliers.

296
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,964
Then move up to a fab,

297
00:10:45,964 --> 00:10:47,930
first with older chips.

298
00:10:47,970 --> 00:10:49,281
And only then,

299
00:10:49,281 --> 00:10:49,790
maybe,

300
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:51,370
the leading edge.

301
00:10:51,370 --> 00:10:53,820
Each step is smaller than the dream.

302
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,237
But each one is real.

303
00:10:56,483 --> 00:10:58,997
So are India's chip plants a failure

304
00:10:58,997 --> 00:11:01,383
because they do not make chips?

305
00:11:01,383 --> 00:11:02,283
No.

306
00:11:02,283 --> 00:11:03,634
They are the first rung of a

307
00:11:03,634 --> 00:11:05,757
ladder that every chip country has had

308
00:11:05,757 --> 00:11:06,743
to climb.

309
00:11:06,843 --> 00:11:08,703
The real test comes in twenty

310
00:11:08,703 --> 00:11:09,378
twenty-eight,

311
00:11:09,378 --> 00:11:11,703
when Dholera is meant to start selling

312
00:11:11,703 --> 00:11:13,233
chips of its own.

313
00:11:13,273 --> 00:11:14,169
Until then,

314
00:11:14,169 --> 00:11:16,695
India is learning the cheapest lesson in

315
00:11:16,695 --> 00:11:17,821
chipmaking first,

316
00:11:17,821 --> 00:11:20,095
how to finish what others started,

317
00:11:20,095 --> 00:11:22,303
before it learns how to start.

318
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:25,031
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

319
00:11:25,031 --> 00:11:27,989
we follow the money behind another hidden

320
00:11:27,989 --> 00:11:30,410
link of the world economy.

321
00:11:30,450 --> 00:11:32,783
This is The Hidden Economics.
